# XDF files are data artifacts, not source code.
#
# Git must not rewrite their line endings. With core.autocrlf=true Git
# normalises text files on commit and converts them back on checkout, which
# silently changes an XDF's bytes and therefore its hash. That matters here
# because these files are validated and distributed by hash:
# out/R0C2J772B_ignition_timing.xdf was inspected in TunerPro in its CRLF
# form, and that CRLF form is the canonical artifact stored in this repository.
#
# '-text' marks these paths as binary for end-of-line purposes: the blob is
# written and checked out byte for byte, so a checkout on Windows and a
# checkout on Linux produce identical files.
#
# The ECU firmware images (*iRom_ori, *iRom_stage2) are already treated as
# binary by content auto-detection and need no rule here.
*.xdf -text